        <h1>How websites get benefit in ranking with page speed optimisation.</h1>
        <p>
            Do you know every millisecond gets counted while analyzing website performance? Your website speed and overall performance determine search engine rankings. So how can your website rank higher? Are there any practical strategies that can be implemented to speed up the success rate of your website? What is the <span style="background-color: rgba(231, 160, 27, 0.582);">importance of website speed?</span> Page Speed Optimization is a unique technique developed to improve website search rankings
            !</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.pagespeedsolution.com/">Site speed optimization service</a> is the ultimate solution to all your questions. Because daily we work on numerous websites and fix their non-performance issues, leading to higher sales and conversions. So what do we do? Here is a blog we want you to read and understand about the key principles of site speed optimization and how it is done. </p>

        <h2>What Are The Strategies To Optimize Your Website and Get Higher Rankings</h2>
        <ol>
            <li><b>Site Audit</b></li>
        <p>Firstly you need to audit your current website performance. Then decide to make changes that improve your site speed loading rate. You can use free tools like PageSpeed Insights that assess your Core Web Vitals on mobile or desktop. It will help you find out your exact performance rate with a score. You can also find the areas of improvement to get a higher score. Gather enough data about your site performance and use it to identify fixes and implement key strategies.
        </p>

<li><b>Fix Potential Issues First</b></li>
        
        <p>After finding the website speed issues, don’t rush. Try not to fix everything together. We recommend you prioritize fixes based on what all matters most to your visitors. There are speed testing tools that provide recommendations and diagnostics, helping you prioritize your optimization efforts. With site speed optimization service, you get a team that will work on your website performance issues and provide faster-loading websites that are more responsive than before and will boost user satisfaction. Ultimately, it will lead to higher search engine rankings.  
        </p>

<li><b>Consider CDN</b></li>
        <p>Managing site data is tricky and needs some skill. If your site is fully loaded with data in one place, your load times suffer. The more internet traffic grows the more issues with improving page speed load time. With the rising global internet traffic, you need more site speed optimization techniques. Here, CDN (Content delivery networks) helps. CDNs use multiple servers to store content replications for multiple locations. CDN will choose the closest server from where the user can visit your site, optimizing content delivery. Well, CDNs are already popular and they carry around 72% of Internet traffic.</p>

<li><b>Image Optimization</b></li>
        <p>Images are meant to improve engagement, however, they can also speed down page loading times with high resolutions. HTTP Archives suggest median image weight on a web page should be over 1000 KB. So compressing images can save weight and time. Several photo editing tools and programs can optimize images for sites. You must choose the best format like WebP format to compress images and avoid losing a better view. You get lossless and loss compression for images.</p>

<li><b>Limit HTTP Requests</b></li>
        <p>Each HTTP requests you make on your site for images, scripts, fonts, etc. will add load time. The bigger the website, the higher the speed load time. Because the HTTP requests stack up, creating a considerable delay between CTR (click-through rate) and actual page loading. But the good news is you can limit the HTTP requests with a strategy and reduce the page speed load time. You can hire a site speed optimization service for the same.</p>


<li><b>Caching </b></li>
        <p>Caching technique pre-loads website content through a browser, enabling it to speed up webpage delivery. Various CMS platforms like WordPress automatically cache the most current versions of the site. You can either reduce or extend the caching timeframe in your CMS settings for content that doesn't change for a long time like static images, JavaScript files, logos, stylesheets, etc. If your CMS does not have this feature, you can install a caching plugin, that provides you with all-inclusive caching optimization. 
        </p>

<li><b>Track 404 Errors</b></li>
        <p>When users try to access the page that you have deleted ‘404 errors or page not found’ occur. When they run into a 404 error page, they will not get access to your site again. So you lose a potential customer here! So first solve 404 errors by running free and external tools to track such results and remove those dead links.</p>


<li><b>Mobile First</b></li>
        <p>Statista found <a href="https://www.statista.com/forecasts/1145773/mobile-internet-users-in-the-united-states" rel="nofollow">the growing number of mobile internet users amounting to 276 mn in 2021. And, it is expected to rise to 296 mn by 2025</a>. More and more people use mobile devices for several needs. Another survey done by Hubspot found that <a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/blog/tabid/6307/bid/5092/how-many-visitors-should-your-site-get.aspx?hubs_content=blog.hubspot.com%2Fwebsite%2Fhow-to-optimize-website-speed&hubs_content-cta=Image%20Source" rel="nofollow">41% of traffic to their site comes from mobile</a>. So more and more users switch to mobile devices for browsing and shopping. Hence, so first try to simply display your desktop site on mobile devices with ease. This will improve your website performance you will be saved from interactivity issues that can frustrate users. Developing a mobile-native website will increase load speed and increase responsiveness.  </p>


<li><b>CMS Migration</b></li>
        <p>To build a website with speed and customize it, you need a robust website builder. However, these website builders may need adequate infrastructure and features to fix slow load time issues. So if you face the same kind of situation, consider CMS migration. Choose the right content management system to improve your website performance and streamline content retrieval. After all, speed matters, and where it doesn't work out, get a robust option that can help you modify site operations and also have an in-built CDN facility.</p>

<li><b>Minify JavaScript and CSS Files</b></li>
        <p>Another way to reduce JavaScipt and CSS file size is through minification. The technique removal of unwanted code such as white space characters, comments, line breaks, extra semicolons, longhand CSS selectors, unused functions, and variables. Working on these elements can reduce file sizes and improve speed load times.</p>


<li><b>Choose Asynchronous Loading</b></li>
        <p>Several files and functions on your website have synchronous loading by default. So they load in an orderly manner on the page. For example, elements load once the script gets fully loaded. This will increase page load time. The good news is you can fix this! You can use CMS platforms that provide in-built features or plugins to perform asynchronous loading for CSS and JavaScirpt elements. This will allow both images and script to load together.</p>



        </ol>
    <div>
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>Faster websites give better results. Because speedier websites display content faster and lower your bounce rates, leading to higher conversions. So if you want to supercharge your website, we can help you. There is a process that we follow as we implement any or all of the above 11 strategies to improve your site speed. Our team of page speed experts can provide a universal solution for your website speed. Our services include all the features that you need for site speed optimization. <span style="background-color: rgba(231, 160, 27, 0.582);">Explore our range of services</span> or contact us today!</p>
